# Accepted crypto call-site exceptions (issue #612).
#
# The `cmd/citecheck` crypto-surface gate enumerates every non-test Go file
# that imports crypto/*, golang.org/x/crypto/*, or a JWT/signing library and
# requires each one to be accounted for by an ASVS V6 row in asvs-l2.md OR by
# an entry here. A file that imports crypto with no V6 row and no entry here
# FAILS the gate, and an entry here whose file no longer imports crypto ALSO
# fails — so this file cannot quietly accumulate dead suppressions, the same
# bidirectional convention as .trivyignore, .grype.yml and
# citation-drift.ignore.
#
# These are NOT crypto-decision call sites: they import a crypto package for a
# reason other than choosing a cryptographic primitive, so no ASVS V6 row
# claims them as surface. Each entry is a decision someone wrote down.
#
# Format:  <backend-relative path>  # why this is not a crypto call site

backend/services/calendar_sync_service.go  # crypto/sha256 over joined event parts as a deterministic dedup/content key for imported calendar events — a stable content hash, not a cryptographic decision (no security property is derived from it)
backend/services/contact_sync_service.go    # crypto/sha256 over the synced contact payload as a change-detection content hash (skip when unchanged) — same non-crypto-decision reasoning as calendar_sync_service.go
backend/services/household_service.go       # crypto/sha256 over address/member keys as deterministic grouping keys for the household suggestion engine — a stable hash key, not a cryptographic decision
backend/services/immich_client.go           # crypto/tls for the outbound Immich transport (TLS config, not a primitive choice) — same class as the other file-integration clients
backend/services/mailer.go                  # crypto/tls for SMTP transport (TLS config, not a primitive choice)
backend/services/paperless_client.go        # crypto/tls for the outbound Paperless-ngx transport (TLS config, not a primitive choice)
backend/services/seafile_client.go          # crypto/tls for the outbound Seafile transport (TLS config, not a primitive choice)
backend/services/webdav_client.go           # crypto/tls for the outbound Nextcloud/WebDAV transport (TLS config, not a primitive choice)
backend/controllers/oidc_controller.go      # crypto/subtle constant-time comparison of OIDC state/nonce cookies — a comparison helper, not a primitive selection; 6.2.8 (constant-time) is out-of-scope L3
backend/controllers/metrics_controller.go   # crypto/subtle constant-time comparison of the METRICS_TOKEN scrape credential (issue #389) — a comparison helper, not a primitive selection; 6.2.8 (constant-time) is out-of-scope L3
backend/middleware/idempotency.go            # crypto/sha256 over method+path+body as a request fingerprint for CON-04 idempotency-key replay (issue #459) — detects a key reused for a different request, a change-detection hash, not a cryptographic decision (same class as contact_sync_service.go)
backend/services/device_grant_service.go    # crypto/rand for the 32-byte device-grant tokens + crypto/sha256 to store their one-way hash — the same mint-then-hash pattern as api_tokens' generateApiToken (controllers/api_token_controller.go), a token-hashing helper, not a primitive-selection decision (no security property is derived from the hash beyond one-way storage)
